{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/24376-questions-about-pacts","id":24376,"title":"Questions about Pacts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-06T08:48:49-08:00","id":24376,"title":"Questions about Pacts","content":"So after reading the rules on pacts there are a few things I'm unclear on that I'd love to get some answers to.<br /> <br /> First, what exactly is the downside of a pact to a demon other than the willpower cost? The rules talk about how demons make sure to make pacts unfair towards the person but I don't understand why? Unless I'm misreading it the stuff a person gets out of a deal isn't provided by the demon at all so there's no incentive to cheat. Like if I make pact with a person to get their spouse I can offer the person 1 dot of resources or 3 dots of resources, 4 dots of striking looks, and anything else I can think of and its actually better for me to make the one that helps them as it costs me less willpower and the universe gives them these things not me. Why bother cheating people when unbalancing it in their favor costs you nothing, makes the pact harder for you to make(greater willpower cost) makes it easier to get a signature and makes them positively inclined towards you? It seems like a really smart idea to just make incredibly unbalanced pacts in the humans favor towards some friends then reap the rewards of powerful allies, make the pacts only last a year and you're pretty much guaranteed they will treat you well to keep the pact renewed. <br /> <br /> Second how much extra stuff can be added in? The big thing I saw nothing about was a time limit before a soul pact can be activated. A lot of demon fiction(Supernatural is what sticks out to me) has the deal with a demon be that you get stuff but that in a year or a decade or so the demon shows up to collect. It seems like a way better way to get someone to sign a soul pact, if they know for sure they get at least certain amount of time to enjoy the benefits. Is it possible to write something like that in, or other conditions like after cashing in a soul pact the demon has to take care of the persons children, or after taking the persons pet as a piece of cover the demon has to treat it well?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/92-ramza","name":"Ramza","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar92_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T09:15:58-08:00","id":24390,"title":"","content":"Demons shortchange people on pacts to create an artificial scarcity in their lives. It gives the people they deal with a need to keep coming back and bargaining away more and more to maintain their benefits over time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T09:16:48-08:00","id":24392,"title":"","content":"for aoulpacts i dont see why you cant put in that it cant be collected for a full year (also normal pacts can have a duration and as you can have both types of pacts with someone it should be possible to even combine them i rhink) brw you mentioning children and spouse reminded me of sth. soulpacts dont transfer memories but ehat about normal ones? thus do you gain the others memories of the spouse you just got for resources? or do you have to guess hmmm the person that is now at the door is my new wife?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T10:15:33-08:00","id":24417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/24376-questions-about-pacts?p=24392#post24392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">for aoulpacts i dont see why you cant put in that it cant be collected for a full year (also normal pacts can have a duration and as you can have both types of pacts with someone it should be possible to even combine them i rhink) brw you mentioning children and spouse reminded me of sth. soulpacts dont transfer memories but ehat about normal ones? thus do you gain the others memories of the spouse you just got for resources? or do you have to guess hmmm the person that is now at the door is my new wife?</div> </div> </div> </div> You do not gain any of their memories, and a demon looking to take someone's soul would be well advised to research the life he plans to take over. Hell, at least learn what your soon to be wife and kids look like. A soul pact should not be taken on lightly, and learning important details about the person whose life you plan to steal is a very important step. (Unless of course, you want to immediately burn all your new cover's bridges, which is something one might do, but it would likely cause some cover breaking points because that's not really something most people do out of nowhere.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T10:38:50-08:00","id":24438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/24376-questions-about-pacts?p=24417#post24417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You do not gain any of their memories, and a demon looking to take someone's soul would be well advised to research the life he plans to take over. Hell, at least learn what your soon to be wife and kids look like. A soul pact should not be taken on lightly, and learning important details about the person whose life you plan to steal is a very important step. (Unless of course, you want to immediately burn all your new cover's bridges, which is something one might do, but it would likely cause some cover breaking points because that's not really something most people do out of nowhere.)</div> </div> </div> </div>exactly for soulpacts but is it the same for normal pacts also?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T16:04:38-08:00","id":24717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/24376-questions-about-pacts?p=24417#post24417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You do not gain any of their memories, and a demon looking to take someone's soul would be well advised to research the life he plans to take over. Hell, at least learn what your soon to be wife and kids look like. A soul pact should not be taken on lightly, and learning important details about the person whose life you plan to steal is a very important step. (Unless of course, you want to immediately burn all your new cover's bridges, which is something one might do, but it would likely cause some cover breaking points because that's not really something most people do out of nowhere.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Or if you're going to be <i>that guy</i> and keep a few extra Soul Pacts lying around so you can afford to go Loud sparingly without sacrificing your favorite skin-suit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T06:30:44-08:00","id":26463,"title":"","content":"Squid: You don't need a soul. 3 cover XP. Burn the thinnest patch-jobs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T17:34:02-08:00","id":26846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/24376-questions-about-pacts?p=26463#post26463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Squid: You don't need a soul. 3 cover XP. Burn the thinnest patch-jobs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fine, fine, be practical and don't eat people willy-nilly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T09:15:53-08:00","id":27248,"title":"","content":"The section on Pacts mentions briefly that the things mortals get out of signing up have to come from somewhere, so I imagine there are at least some demons who would feel guilty about cheating innocent bystanders out of their money. Beyond that, my guess is that that level of juggling resources around could get the God Machine's attention; I might even make a house rule in my games wherein if the mortal's side of the Pact exceeds the demon's by X, a Compromise roll must be made. Aiden's answer about artificial scarcity sounds quite reasonable as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T10:29:14-08:00","id":27295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/24376-questions-about-pacts?p=26463#post26463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Squid: You don't need a soul. 3 cover XP. Burn the thinnest patch-jobs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nobody is going to miss some homeless beggar. And if it happens to actually be a TV correspondent posing as a homeless beggar... well... oops? (If you don't get it, watch last night's Colbert Report.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;Seven deadly sins/Seven ways to win/Seven holy paths to hell/And your trip begins/Seven downward slopes/Seven bloodied hopes/Seven are your burning fires/Seven your desires&quot; \u2014 Iron Maiden,</i> Moonchild","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1122-the-grim-lich","name":"The Grim Lich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T19:04:30-08:00","id":30203,"title":"","content":"Different Pact related question: I see no reason or rule to prevent a Demon from making a pact that grants a mortal a Supernatural Merit (like Aura Reading or Psychokinesis) or even a Hunter Endowment (though I CAN think of like a dozen in-character reasons that this would be a terrible idea for both sides). <br /> <br /> But what about granting something that can be bought with Merit points, that isn't a Merit PER SAY.<br /> There is, after all, a LOT of story and legend built up around the concept of wizards or, perhaps, MAGES trafficking with Demons for power.<br /> What would you think about allowing a Demon to forge a Greater pact (+3 weight/grant asset) to grant a Mage 1 Arete (or alternatively another supernatural it's relative power stat)?<br /> Get a Mage to do you some major favors in return, and of coarse also get stuck being your protector because if the contract gets shredded BOTH ends of the deal go out. <br /> I'm pretty sure it's not supported by the rules as written, but would you allow it in your game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T22:18:58-08:00","id":30275,"title":"","content":"GMC's Supernatural Merits? Maybe. I think that, generally, a Demon (i.e. Unchained) needs to have a supernatural ability in order to grant it to another (see also: Gadget creation). I could also see an Exploit or Interlock based on the metaphysics behind Inflict Stigmata or Hellhound that could grant supernatural merits. Hunter Endowments? Almost certainly not, but see next paragraph. Anything else? No. There are demons who bear no relation to the Unchained, after all[1]. <br /> <br /> I wouldn't allow a Demon to grant Endowments immediately, but\u2014by granting Social Merits\u2014they'd help with the social engineering to get access to them. I don't know Hunter, but the impression I've gotten is that most Endowments represent organizational resources, which means that a Demon could speed up becoming a Hunter in that Conspiracy. Once you're in the Conspiracy and have at least one dot of the Endowment, I might allow a Demon to improve it using Pacts. I need to learn more about Endowments. <br /> <br /> [1] For Mages making deals with demons, see Summoners, Inferno, or other sources whose names escape me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1231,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1231-gapb","user":"gapb","date":".  Clarification, and concession. 12-15-2013, 03:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1231-gapb","name":"gapb","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T02:30:35-08:00","id":30343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TiwazTyrsfist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/24376-questions-about-pacts?p=30203#post30203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Different Pact related question: I see no reason or rule to prevent a Demon from making a pact that grants a mortal a Supernatural Merit (like Aura Reading or Psychokinesis) or even a Hunter Endowment (though I CAN think of like a dozen in-character reasons that this would be a terrible idea for both sides).</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep in mind that nothing is created <i>ex nihilo</i> with Demonic Pacts, it always comes from somewhere. So I agree, there shouldn't be a rule or reason to prevent a mortal gaining a Supernatural merit, but <i>something</i> happens to make that mortal have that merit. The better question is, who lost that merit? And what would they do to get it back?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TiwazTyrsfist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/24376-questions-about-pacts?p=30203#post30203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But what about granting something that can be bought with Merit points, that isn't a Merit PER SAY.<br /> There is, after all, a LOT of story and legend built up around the concept of wizards or, perhaps, MAGES trafficking with Demons for power.<br /> What would you think about allowing a Demon to forge a Greater pact (+3 weight/grant asset) to grant a Mage 1 Arete (or alternatively another supernatural it's relative power stat)?<br /> Get a Mage to do you some major favors in return, and of coarse also get stuck being your protector because if the contract gets shredded BOTH ends of the deal go out.<br /> I'm pretty sure it's not supported by the rules as written, but would you allow it in your game?</div> </div> </div> </div>New World of Darkness Mages use Gnosis, not Arete, but you're right that a Power Stat should be available for pacts. It'd definitely be a Greater factor, but again, it <i>comes from somewhere.</i> Who loses that power stat? How would the person who lost it, track it? And how far would they go to get it back?<br /> <br /> <br /> Just remember Rule 2: <b>Never Let Mechanics get in the way of a Good Story.</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T07:19:38-08:00","id":30407,"title":"","content":"Supernatural merits would come from an unlocked strain of DNA, and, given that Gnosis is knowledge, and you can impart it with pacts without someone else becoming dumber...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T07:23:57-08:00","id":30408,"title":"","content":"About this whole matter of granting a Power Stat, why not make it where the Demon has to go out and steal it in some fashion or else engineer someone losing it, in some fashion. This could be the basis of a solid story arc that nets the Demon the aforementioned Supernatural Guardian for the contract...and also of all the contracts, if done right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T07:56:33-08:00","id":30420,"title":"","content":"Bit of a stretch, IMO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T09:36:31-08:00","id":30463,"title":"","content":"That may be, but I always allow the players to do what they wish if I think that it is something worthy of a great story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T12:04:36-08:00","id":30514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/24376-questions-about-pacts?p=30407#post30407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Supernatural merits would come from an unlocked strain of DNA, and, given that Gnosis is knowledge, and you can impart it with pacts without someone else becoming dumber...</div> </div> </div> </div>Both true, but question: How would the player unlock that DNA? How would the player have the Supernal knowledge (Gnosis) to impart? In my reading of the book, <i>ex nihilo</i> creation is beyond even the God Machine, it requires Infrastructure to enact any changes.<br /> <br /> Here's how I think both of our stances can be reconciled: The &quot;balance&quot; is maintained by a debt/trade-off in another form rather than another's loss. An Awakened's Gnosis is increased through inspiration via tutelage by another Awakened. The enlightened Awakened now has whatever debt to the mentor he would otherwise, while the Demon is the one who made it happen. A Forsaken's Primal Urge is increased by his interactions with Spirit Courts, gaining him whatever reputation goes along with that, for good or ill. (My apologies if this isn't how that happens, I haven't read W:tF in a while.)<br /> <br /> About mortals gaining supernatural merits, suddenly they are in the supernatural world, if only tangentially of it. Their newfound merits make them quite useful to supernatural beings looking for disposable resources or resources that aren't nominally traceable to them. (When someone realizes their mind has been plumbed for information, they don't think Sin-Eater or Promethean, and when someone realizes they are being spied upon through projected senses they don't think Forsaken.)<br /> <br /> Do the players get involved in these dealings beyond their &quot;brokering&quot; the underlying changes in the universe? Do they involve the others in their espionage? That could lead in of itself to a great story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T18:43:59-08:00","id":30680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paddon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/24376-questions-about-pacts?p=30343#post30343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New World of Darkness Mages use Gnosis, not Arete, but you're right that a Power Stat should be available for pacts. It'd definitely be a Greater factor, but again, it <i>comes from somewhere.</i> Who loses that power stat? How would the person who lost it, track it? And how far would they go to get it back?<br /> <br /> <br /> Just remember Rule 2: <b>Never Let Mechanics get in the way of a Good Story.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>And now you've given me an idea for a Mage (or Werewolf, or Vampire, or Changeling, or other supernatural) game. The [group noun here] discovers that, overnight, they've lost some of their power. Something's stolen it, and they need to get it back... otherwise, their enemies will basically be able to run roughshod over them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;Seven deadly sins/Seven ways to win/Seven holy paths to hell/And your trip begins/Seven downward slopes/Seven bloodied hopes/Seven are your burning fires/Seven your desires&quot; \u2014 Iron Maiden,</i> Moonchild","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1122-the-grim-lich","name":"The Grim Lich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-16T01:42:29-08:00","id":30840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Both true, but question: How would the player unlock that DNA? How would the player have the Supernal knowledge (Gnosis) to impart? In my reading of the book, <i>ex nihilo</i> creation is beyond even the God Machine, it requires Infrastructure to enact any changes. </div> </div> </div>If I actually knew the answer to this question, I wouldn't be wasting my time replying to this, instead of dunno, reading the mind of people to figure out their bank account pins.<br /> <br /> The pact re-writes reality. That's all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-16T16:45:22-08:00","id":31316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Grim Lich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/24376-questions-about-pacts?p=30680#post30680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And now you've given me an idea for a Mage (or Werewolf, or Vampire, or Changeling, or other supernatural) game. The [group noun here] discovers that, overnight, they've lost some of their power. Something's stolen it, and they need to get it back... otherwise, their enemies will basically be able to run roughshod over them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Post it as an Actual Play and we're even <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/24376-questions-about-pacts?p=30840#post30840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I actually knew the answer to this question, I wouldn't be wasting my time replying to this, instead of dunno, reading the mind of people to figure out their bank account pins.<br /> The pact re-writes reality. That's all.</div> </div> </div> </div>The answer to the question is: Plot. Hand-waving has it's place, as does making the players participate in writing the story too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-16T18:04:36-08:00","id":31364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paddon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/24376-questions-about-pacts?p=30343#post30343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New World of Darkness Mages use Gnosis, not Arete, but you're right that a Power Stat should be available for pacts. It'd definitely be a Greater factor, but again, it <i>comes from somewhere.</i> Who loses that power stat? How would the person who lost it, track it? And how far would they go to get it back?</div> </div> </div> </div>Though this very well could be the case in any specific game world, I was under the impression (from my cursory examination of the document) that this is not in fact objectively true. While some Demons -speculate- that pacts must 'take' from somewhere in the universe to power the hack, others might disagree or suggest that the system somehow just cheats more resources into reality. Is this not the case?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-16T18:09:11-08:00","id":31366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/24376-questions-about-pacts?p=31364#post31364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Though this very well could be the case in any specific game world, I was under the impression (from my cursory examination of the document) that this is not in fact objectively true. While some Demons -speculate- that pacts must 'take' from somewhere in the universe to power the hack, others might disagree or suggest that the system somehow just cheats more resources into reality. Is this not the case?</div> </div> </div> </div>The speculation is that pacts work on similar principles to Embeds \u2014 &quot;[using] established metaphysical pathways to attract the kind of change [they need].&quot;<br /> <br /> That the universe balances the books on anything provided by a pact is <i>cited as support for that theory.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T10:28:59-08:00","id":31761,"title":"","content":"Along those lines, I asked this question in another thread but kinda phrased it badly : Could a human be made into a vampire with a pact?<br /> <br /> When you secure bits of cover via a pact... say, a best friend... are you obligated to use the best friend IMMEDIATELY? Or can you 'store' it in paper form for trade later? Let's say you trade somebody for a 'negative' life aspect, like a horrible ex. If you intend to barter that bit of cover to an agency, can you do so without having to have a horrible ex yourself for a while? Does the person who gave up the ex get the 'benifit' of the ex until the deal is 'cashed in'?<br /> <br /> Example :<br /> <br /> Joe Demon makes a deal with Frank for his disabled sister, who's a quadrapeligic anyway that he feels burdened by. This life-defining sibling is a juicy cover element that can provide the backbone for an entire identity. Joe wants to sell this to his local agency. When Joe presents the contract to Frank and Frank signs his sister away, does Frank's sister 'vanish' until somebody cashes in the contract? Does the sister become Joe Demon's sister, obligated Joe to be her 'nurse' until he can offload the contract to agency?<br /> <br /> I've considered lots of different ways of handling this, balanced towards realism and playability, and I'd like to see what the forum thinks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T12:03:38-08:00","id":31818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/24376-questions-about-pacts?p=31761#post31761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Along those lines, I asked this question in another thread but kinda phrased it badly : Could a human be made into a vampire with a pact?</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally, no. The impression I've gotten is that you should assume that members of one Greater Supernatural Template can't grant or empower other Greater Supernatural Templates\u2014unless explicitly noted otherwise. This said, as Paddon said earlier, never let mechanics get in the way of a good story. Go with the option you think is best for your Chronicle.[1]<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/24376-questions-about-pacts?p=31761#post31761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you secure bits of cover via a pact... say, a best friend... are you obligated to use the best friend IMMEDIATELY? Or can you 'store' it in paper form for trade later? Let's say you trade somebody for a 'negative' life aspect, like a horrible ex. If you intend to barter that bit of cover to an agency, can you do so without having to have a horrible ex yourself for a while? Does the person who gave up the ex get the 'benifit' of the ex until the deal is 'cashed in'?</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that soul pacts are tradable until cashed in, I'd handle it the same way. You can 'store' the pact and the cover element provided, but until then the pact's dormant. To use your example, Frank's sister remains Frank's sister, and thus Frank's burden, until someone calls in the pact and adopts the Cover of &quot;has a quadriplegic sister.&quot; Frank gets the other benefits of the deal right away, though, if any.<br /> ---------<br /> [1]Twist: the Demon\u2014via Pacts, Exploits, and/or Interlocks\u2014makes the signatory a blood-drinking undead immortal, but not a Vampire proper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1231,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1231-gapb","user":"gapb","date":". 12-17-2013, 03:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1231-gapb","name":"gapb","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T14:19:55-08:00","id":31891,"title":"","content":"My issue with this is complexity.<br /> <br /> Joe Demon : So, I take the sister, and you get the showbiz job. Done.<br /> Frank : Wait, my sister is still here.<br /> Joe : Yeah. You have custodianship until I cash in.<br /> Frank: When will that be?<br /> Joe : Potentially never.<br /> Frank : Are you gonna let me know?<br /> Joe : Maybe.<br /> <br /> Later...<br /> <br /> Mary Demon : Hey, you got a sister to trade me?<br /> Joe : I -think- so. Let me text my client to see if he's still alive... ah, shit, he's at the basketball game. Can I getcha later?<br /> <br /> Later...<br /> <br /> Joe : Sorry Marry, turns out my clients sister got hit by a car a few days ago, so...<br /> <br /> In the end, it creates a kinda overcomplicated spiraling web of considerations, particularly if you're dealing with multiple pacts over multiple demons. To a large degree it seems more simple to just 'render' the Cover down into a 'Trading Card' - the cover becomes part of the 'character' of the Contract, and thus kinda vanishes from reality. Then it can be traded much more freely.<br /> <br /> That's the solution I settled on, not to suggest it's canon or appropriate or anything, that's just what I did and the reasons why.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T15:25:23-08:00","id":31937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/24376-questions-about-pacts?p=31761#post31761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you secure bits of cover via a pact... say, a best friend... are you obligated to use the best friend IMMEDIATELY? Or can you 'store' it in paper form for trade later? Let's say you trade somebody for a 'negative' life aspect, like a horrible ex. If you intend to barter that bit of cover to an agency, can you do so without having to have a horrible ex yourself for a while? Does the person who gave up the ex get the 'benifit' of the ex until the deal is 'cashed in'?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a lot clearer for soul pacts than for lesser pacts, but looking at the text and the way pacts are described in general, it sounds like writing a check. The mortal gets whatever they asked for the moment the contract is signed and they keep it for the duration of the contract, but the Demon can hold off on depositing the check and collecting their fee (the Cover) until they need it, or until they decide to give it to another Demon.<br /> <br /> The text on soul pacts seems to imply that Demons have to collect on lesser pacts immediately, but that doesn't seem right.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/24376-questions-about-pacts?p=31891#post31891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Joe : Sorry Marry, turns out my clients sister got hit by a car a few days ago, so...</div> </div> </div> </div>Now that I think about it, this raises an interesting question. What happens if a mortal becomes unable to fulfill their end of the contract after it was signed in good faith?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":54,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","user":"Tiresias","date":". 12-17-2013, 06:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T15:59:37-08:00","id":31961,"title":"","content":"@MissMaddy:<br /> <br /> First Case: That's what happens when you get the cover XP. The deal isn't cashed until you spend it.<br /> <br /> Second Case: Demons, generally speaking, don't deal with humans over already signed pacts. They would deal with the one who &quot;holds the rights&quot;. Now... what would happen if two demons sign the same pact with a human? would the human benefit twice? I'd say yes. And when one of them cashes it? The other one becomes null and void. First dibs here.<br /> <br /> Third case: That would null the contract, plain and simple. For the mortal as well; unless the demon gets a background with his dead sister. Serves the same. He gets a tomb to visit. I'd lower the XP price then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T16:44:40-08:00","id":31993,"title":"","content":"Hmm. I have issues with this.<br /> <br /> Second case ; I dislike the idea that humans can 'cheat' demons by double-dealing and making them fight with one another. I'd suggest, rather, that demons DO in fact remove something 'physical' to them when the contract is signed ; such that, future demons could note 'hmm, you can't sell me your sister, you don't HAVE a sister'. But this does in fact presume rendering down the soul-piece in question to a trading card. Once the victim 'sells' his sister, she vanishes from reality and effectively becomes a symbolic representation until she is given to somebody else or used herself.<br /> <br /> Exceptionally disruptive 'vanishings' might attract the attention of the God Machine, so doing this to Barack Obama's brother... and making Obama vanish into a trading card... is probably unwise, though the God Machine is robust enough to generally speaking absorb this sort of thing without too much difficulty.<br /> <br /> Third case ; this irritates me because it proposes that a demon with lots of Cover identities to sell is inordinantly concerned with maintaining those cover identities in saleable form ; such a demon could rapidly be drawn into an endless downward spiral of minutia, as he struggles to keep marriages together, elderly relatives cared for, pets well fed, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T17:58:58-08:00","id":32036,"title":"","content":"Mortals and demons have to be able to fulfill their contracts, so it shouldn't be possible for mortals to double-deal. Once the mortal agrees to sell his sister, she belongs to the Demon even if it just shelves the contract for a while. The mortal shouldn't be able to sell his sister to another Demon in the meantime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-18T02:56:28-08:00","id":32250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Second case ; I dislike the idea that humans can 'cheat' demons by double-dealing and making them fight with one another. I'd suggest, rather, that demons DO in fact remove something 'physical' to them when the contract is signed ; such that, future demons could note 'hmm, you can't sell me your sister, you don't HAVE a sister' </div> </div> </div>Not if it's not cashed.<br /> <br /> I'm fine with Mortals being able to double deal, because, let's face it. There's plenty of stories where the Demon gets outsmarted. Also, to clarify? If the person doesn't has the sister, it means the pact was cashed in already. If the pact exists merely as experience still? cool. I'd like to see the second demon noticing, at first glance, he's gonna get cheated.<br /> <br /> It makes for a good story, if anything. A Temporal Agency which is giving away more than one contract? Awesome.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But this does in fact presume rendering down the soul-piece in question to a trading card. Once the victim 'sells' his sister, she vanishes from reality and effectively becomes a symbolic representation until she is given to somebody else or used herself. </div> </div> </div>This is not the case. If the pact isn't cashed, life goes on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mortals and demons have to be able to fulfill their contracts, so it shouldn't be possible for mortals to double-deal. Once the mortal agrees to sell his sister, she belongs to the Demon even if it just shelves the contract for a while. The mortal shouldn't be able to sell his sister to another Demon in the meantime. </div> </div> </div>Again, the first and second demonic signataries got the rights to the sister until she's collected. Consider that if all your lesser, non-soul pacts should be cashed in immediately, crafting a patch up cover would be a nightmarish exercise.<br /> <br /> I'd much prefer to get several contracts, then cash them in together: say, 15 cover experiences for a 5 Cover new patch-job existance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-18T14:46:58-08:00","id":32727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/24376-questions-about-pacts?p=32250#post32250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm fine with Mortals being able to double deal, because, let's face it. There's plenty of stories where the Demon gets outsmarted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that how <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Constantine#Occult_.22hero.22\" target=\"_blank\">John Constantine</a> got out of having the First of the Fallen torture him in Hell? <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wikipedia</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Slowly dying from cancer, John hatched a plan to save himself from eternal torment. He secretly sold his soul to the other two Lords of Hell. When they discovered Constantine's actions they realized that they could not allow him to die, or else they would be forced to go to all-out war over his soul \u2014 a war whose only winner would be &quot;the Lord of the Hosts&quot; (i.e. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/God\" target=\"_blank\">God</a>) and his <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Angel\" target=\"_blank\">angels</a>. However, they were also far too stubborn and proud to enter anything resembling an alliance. As a result, they were forced to cure John of his cancer.</div> </div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-18T18:50:44-08:00","id":32899,"title":"","content":"I'd also say, that if someone sells their sister and the sister dies before patch installation, that's fine. The dead sister is still part of their life story. Arguably, it becomes more convenient for the demon at that point, because none of the sister's friends will come to visit her and ask how her brother is and then get weirded out when she says she only has a sister. (Assuming the demon in a feminine Cover for the sake of this example). And it's as natural for a lot of people to avoid graves of their loved ones as visit them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T01:51:14-08:00","id":33014,"title":"","content":"See, the way it's written indicates to me that the only contract type where &quot;payment&quot; is held in abeyance are soul pacts, otherwise it's effects are immediate (or at least <i>in motion</i>, in the case of things that take time to come to fruition like Resources, etc.). You say &quot;money for sister&quot;, he agrees, you sign, his bank account goes up, you get a sister and a piece of paper (or other media) holding the reality code that says <i>the demon who possesses this has a sister</i> which he can later trade. Until the moment the mortal signed the contract, she was his sister; from then until the moment you trade the pact away she's -your- sister.<br /> <br /> Yes, that means if you want to have a sister who's still alive - whether or not you plan to trade her away - you best take care of her; same as you would if you were cultivating a cover as Joe the Criminal who an arms dealer friend, Joe would have to decide whether or not his arms dealer friend was worth protecting and cultivating, even if the demon being Joe differs from time to time. Aside from the occasional person created whole cloth for a cover, people live their lives even if they're metaphysically tied to a Demon. If the cover is destroyed, or if you use houserules for things like dormant covers or the like, then reality isn't rewritten that your sister or arms dealer doesn't exist anymore, it's rewritten in such a way that she doesn't have a brother or the dealer doesn't remember Joe.<br /> <br /> I'd rather deal with the complications and bookkeeping of assuming everyone stays alive even if some of their memories are rewritten than removing them whole cloth out of reality and having to dealt with the bookkeeping associated with <i>those holes</i>. It's easier for me to keep track of. Also, I'm not a fan of people disappearing wholesale if they've been contracted away until it's fufilled because that's a way for demons to remove obstacles by dealing with people connected to those obstacles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T04:44:22-08:00","id":33068,"title":"","content":"Kirby: Again, if that's how it works? Patchwork Covers are a nightmare to produce.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T06:00:03-08:00","id":33106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/24376-questions-about-pacts?p=33068#post33068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kirby: Again, if that's how it works? Patchwork Covers are a nightmare to produce.</div> </div> </div> </div>They aren't simple, no, but I'm not sure what makes it a nightmare. I mean, it's basically just like how the relationships of everyone else goes, only you get to pick and choose which ones you want to even have before you get to the choice that everyone else has: whether or not to put time and effort into a relationship (or other facet of reality).<br /> <br /> If you're talking about OOC, I still think you're overstating it. Some notecards or a copy of notepad can theoretically make keeping track of different pacts a breeze. &quot;Traded Dan the ability to walk for his ex-wife Sarah, 2xp&quot;, &quot;Traded Jimmy +3 Resources for his criminal record&quot;, etc. If you want to do what I'd do, then I'd probably work up a name, a current look, and then paper clip, staple, or if it's electronic paste in the different parts that you're incorporating into a specific cover.<br /> <br /> (This should be where I point out that I'd personally rule that you can combine any of the XP into the cover but you can't remove the pieces once you've applied them. If I decide Joe the Criminal is going to have Sarah as an ex-wife and Jimmy's criminal record, I can't just pull them out once I've spent the XP on raising the cover. That's a little further into modularity than I'm willing to go. One of these days I should really type up the list of houserules and tweaks I've considered for the pact system.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":451,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","user":"Kirby Jerusalem","date":". 12-19-2013, 09:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T07:28:52-08:00","id":33168,"title":"","content":"It's a nightmare in the sense that it's either A) Genuinely a nightmare, because you force the player to ACTUALLY RP all the annoying minutia that would be accompanying these life fragments... or B) Not really a nightmare but kinda a nightmare for the ST, because you just off-screen all that shit so it's not relevent anyway, but having all these extra characters/ factors you gotta remember in every plot is really irritating.<br /> <br /> That's why I favor option C, because, it gets back to the game quickly and without that much trouble.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T15:04:17-08:00","id":33440,"title":"","content":"I mean both IC and OOC.<br /> <br /> And, again, if the pact is still in the form of XP, it's not part of any Cover, and it can be traded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T17:49:27-08:00","id":33570,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/24376-questions-about-pacts?p=33168#post33168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a nightmare in the sense that it's either A) Genuinely a nightmare, because you force the player to ACTUALLY RP all the annoying minutia that would be accompanying these life fragments... or B) Not really a nightmare but kinda a nightmare for the ST, because you just off-screen all that shit so it's not relevent anyway, but having all these extra characters/ factors you gotta remember in every plot is really irritating.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see it mostly being a matter of B* but with even less fuss than what you're saying here. First, unless your characters are trying to be tricky and solve problems and obstacles with better leverage through well placed pacts (which is entirely valid and fun as hell) the NPCs probably aren't going to be interacting with your plot unless you want them to. Second, I'd honestly expect a lot of the onus of record keeping and remembering to be on the players since this is their pact, so as long as you're prepared for &quot;wait a minute, we can get guns from my contact since I haven't traded him away!&quot; then you can probably deal with 90% of the aggravation that's going to come up with pacts.<br /> <br /> I still don't see how this is much more involved than any other time a PC hunts down an NPC contact or whatever, except in this case the PC might even have better documentation!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/24376-questions-about-pacts?p=33440#post33440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, again, if the pact is still in the form of XP, it's not part of any Cover, and it can be traded.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright, I'm still not seeing how this is an issue. I'd say if you're not spending it immediately on a cover then the cover &quot;affected&quot; is the one of the signatory until it's spent or traded away.<br /> <br /> The demon as Miles trades a mortal for his sister, expecting to spend it on a new cover named Joe. As soon as it's signed, the sister recognizes Miles as her brother instead of the signing mortal. If the demon spends the XP on his Joe cover, then reality shifts and she recognizes Joe as her brother. If he trades it to Tim, then Tim's the brother, and so on.<br /> <br /> Again, I'd rather deal with a couple of NPCs having altered memories rather than trying to patch the hole of a removed NPC every time someone made a pact or what happens when they're brought back. Less headache there, in my opinion.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> * Except for when you or the player care enough to get involved because either it's a good story, setting up for a plot hook or because the player likes the NPC/whatever enough to interact with it on his own time. Then you get A.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T18:03:08-08:00","id":33580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Alright, I'm still not seeing how this is an issue. I'd say if you're not spending it immediately on a cover then the cover &quot;affected&quot; is the one of the signatory until it's spent or traded away. </div> </div> </div>That's even <b>more </b>of a headache.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T15:05:20-08:00","id":34104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/24376-questions-about-pacts?p=33580#post33580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's even <b>more </b>of a headache.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not at all. Here's how I'd run it:<br /> <br /> Let's say a player gets five Cover aspects from various Pacts: Jimmy's sister, Mordechai's rabbi, James' schizophrenia, Alice's totes BFF, and Tammy's job.<br /> <br /> When the player bargains for these, the player gets a notecard with &quot;Jimmy's sister&quot; another with &quot;Mordechai's Rabbi&quot;, etc., and how much Cover XP they are worth. These are kept with the character sheet.<br /> <br /> If a Cover aspect is traded to an NPC, the player hands that notecard to the Storyteller. If an aspect is traded to another player, the notecard is handed to the other player.<br /> <br /> If the Cover aspect is folded into a Cover, that aspect is written into the Cover's backstory, the XP is applied, and the notecard is handed to the ST. These held notecards are now plothooks for the ST to use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T17:56:45-08:00","id":34197,"title":"","content":"I've been thinking that after something's been bargained away it's just the relationship that goes into holding - the mortal sees immediate change. So if you buy Alice's abusive relationship with her boyfriend Bob, she isn't his girlfriend after she signs the pact. Until that pact is incorporated into a cover, Bob doesn't have a girlfriend. His memory's fairly foggy about it. There's a soft time limit here - if Bob processes that he's single and gets into a new relationship, activating the pact is going to be more confusing and risky when Bob suddenly has two girlfriends. But maybe Bob juggling two girls is believable. The bigger risk is if you buy the care of a dying relative and then don't show up to keep them alive. Or if you buy someone's job, it's not going to be long before it gets filled. Being the second guy to show up for one job is the kind of thing that draws the attention of the God-Machine. So in this setup there are some cover elements that are relatively easy to bank and trade - personal history especially - and some that are a lot harder, mostly involving persistent relationships.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-21T00:38:51-08:00","id":34339,"title":"","content":"That's essentially how I'd run it. Not all Cover aspects are equal... some are perfectly fine to keep in stasis for a while, others don't quite work that way. That's a case-by-case decision depending on what makes sense for that particular Cover aspect. IMHO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/635-slaunyeh","name":"Slaunyeh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar635_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T05:39:48-08:00","id":35519,"title":"","content":"Not quite a Pacts question here, but close enough.<br /> <br /> I know Demons can trade/give one another Covers. Does it say anywhere how this is done - do they hand over the relevant Pact-paperwork (which. for their 'starting' Cover or one they angel-jacked, logically doesn't exist)? Is it a written Pact of sorts as well? I've not read the googledoc cover to cover (pun unintended) yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T09:27:22-08:00","id":35627,"title":"","content":"Apparently you hand out the paper work (yes, you need a signed document, in blood, if it's a soul pact) and then the holding demon goes and collects (touches the subject, spends one Aether and he's obliterated into the cover)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T16:01:07-08:00","id":35871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/24376-questions-about-pacts?p=35627#post35627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apparently you hand out the paper work (yes, you need a signed document, in blood, if it's a soul pact) and then the holding demon goes and collects (touches the subject, spends one Aether and he's obliterated into the cover)</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you have a page reference? Does it address other sorts of Covers?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T17:33:59-08:00","id":35940,"title":"","content":"Right in the section.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Just Sign Here\u2026</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like a car title, a pact is transferable. Desperation or desire may see a demon want something more than the pact they signed, meaning they will need to make another deal. Some Agencies will buy a contract from such a demon and resell it or seek out the mortal to \u201crenegotiate\u201d the terms of the deal. Demons also love to manipulate or buy pacts from another demon in order to gain a competitive edge.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T02:49:03-08:00","id":36848,"title":"","content":"Pacts talks about gaining health, referring to Stamina. But there is no &quot;Attribute (mortal only)&quot; benefit in pacts. O.o<br /> <br /> They also talk about events, but there are no events in the Cover benefit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T04:16:53-08:00","id":36858,"title":"","content":"Actually I think the &quot;health&quot; just refers to getting cured of disease etc, and as for &quot;events&quot;, that's stuff like how they got the resources, status, fame or whatnot. It is all natural you know, stuff that Could happen <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T09:18:23-08:00","id":37366,"title":"","content":"So, say you made a pact, which gives you 1 cover XP. Duration: One week. What happens when the duration expires? is it the same as if the contract was destroyed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T10:05:44-08:00","id":37381,"title":"","content":"Some sort of option should probably exist for radical physical transformation beyond the 'Striking Looks' merit... why is it that a guy can ask to be a rock star (allies, fame, resources) but not ask to be a strapping lumberjack (str, dex, sta all 4?).<br /> <br /> Seems a perfectly valid and in-theme type of wish to make, although dangerous for balance in mixed games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T10:15:18-08:00","id":37384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/24376-questions-about-pacts?p=37366#post37366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, say you made a pact, which gives you 1 cover XP. Duration: One week. What happens when the duration expires? is it the same as if the contract was destroyed?</div> </div> </div> </div>They answered that here on the forums. I believe it was said that a pact like that doesn't provide truly solid cover \u2014 can't be Burned to Go Loud, for instance \u2014 but it does work as a throwaway identity so that you don't have to lug around your main identity. I think they likened it to a fake mustache.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;Seven deadly sins/Seven ways to win/Seven holy paths to hell/And your trip begins/Seven downward slopes/Seven bloodied hopes/Seven are your burning fires/Seven your desires&quot; \u2014 Iron Maiden,</i> Moonchild","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1122-the-grim-lich","name":"The Grim Lich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T11:20:38-08:00","id":37415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Grim Lich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/24376-questions-about-pacts?p=37384#post37384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They answered that here on the forums. I believe it was said that a pact like that doesn't provide truly solid cover \u2014 can't be Burned to Go Loud, for instance \u2014 but it does work as a throwaway identity so that you don't have to lug around your main identity. I think they likened it to a fake mustache.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's confusing. A dot of cover is 3 Cover XPs. I'm getting 1, likely storing it for a patchwork. Say I take 15, enough to craft myself a nice patchwork cover. What happens when the pacts which consolidate it begin to unravel, on their own expired durations?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T15:46:26-08:00","id":37531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/24376-questions-about-pacts?p=37415#post37415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's confusing. A dot of cover is 3 Cover XPs. I'm getting 1, likely storing it for a patchwork. Say I take 15, enough to craft myself a nice patchwork cover. What happens when the pacts which consolidate it begin to unravel, on their own expired durations?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's just the thing, based on the explanation provided, you can't do that at all unless the duration is permanent.<br /> <br /> Personally, I've decided that the best solution is to assume the zero-cost option is 'permanent' and then charge for the difference between the timespan the mortal and demon get the benefits. Makes deals that keep 'em coming back for more cost more (unless the Demon sweetens the pot).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T23:06:36-08:00","id":39175,"title":"","content":"When making a soul pact the demon loses a dot of willpower. Do they also lose a dot in resolve or composure? If not how much experience does regaining a dot of willpower cost?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1151-walkingeye","name":"WalkingEye","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1151_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T00:07:00-08:00","id":39207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/24376-questions-about-pacts?p=37415#post37415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's confusing. A dot of cover is 3 Cover XPs. I'm getting 1, likely storing it for a patchwork. Say I take 15, enough to craft myself a nice patchwork cover. What happens when the pacts which consolidate it begin to unravel, on their own expired durations?</div> </div> </div> </div>Simple! Temporary pacts no longer function that way. I've been meaning to tell you for a while but I can't find a cite for the life of me.<br /> <br /> Luckily, the PDF just came out!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pg.193</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a demon gains Cover via a temporary pact, instead of granting Cover Experiences the pact grants a thin, transient identity that functions as a one-dot Cover. It cannot be improved, and crumbles if anything occurs that would reduce the Cover rating (this also ends the pact). The pseudo-Cover is always tied to the Pactbound in some way.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T04:59:36-08:00","id":39320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/24376-questions-about-pacts?p=39207#post39207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Luckily, the PDF just came out!</div> </div> </div> </div> I was really hoping they'd be a little less vague on that when it came out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T07:09:53-08:00","id":39357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/24376-questions-about-pacts?p=39207#post39207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Simple! Temporary pacts no longer function that way. I've been meaning to tell you for a while but I can't find a cite for the life of me.<br /> <br /> Luckily, the PDF just came out!<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>that means though that you need to be able to acquire a new cover if you go for temporary pacts (and get something out fo them) else you get a 1 dot cover cant use it and thus must dispose it before you get it so to say?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T11:46:03-08:00","id":39507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/24376-questions-about-pacts?p=39357#post39357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> that means though that you need to be able to acquire a new cover if you go for temporary pacts (and get something out fo them) else you get a 1 dot cover cant use it and thus must dispose it before you get it so to say?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, if you want to get Cover for it (as opposed to a temporary cult or something) then by the book you need to have a slot open to use it as a burner cover.<br /> <br /> If you're playing around with the idea of active and dormant covers like I am, though, you could make one and have it around just in case. Just make sure you use it by the Use By date.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T11:54:22-08:00","id":39511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WalkingEye</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/24376-questions-about-pacts?p=39175#post39175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When making a soul pact the demon loses a dot of willpower. Do they also lose a dot in resolve or composure? If not how much experience does regaining a dot of willpower cost?</div> </div> </div> </div>They do not, and regaining the dot costs one Experience. It's a footnote between the Experience Costs chart and the start of the Agendas section.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T11:59:41-08:00","id":39517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/24376-questions-about-pacts?p=39507#post39507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, if you want to get Cover for it (as opposed to a temporary cult or something) then by the book you need to have a slot open to use it as a burner cover.<br /> <br /> If you're playing around with the idea of active and dormant covers like I am, though, you could make one and have it around just in case. Just make sure you use it by the Use By date.</div> </div> </div> </div>question there you still can't go loud with them can you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T08:35:49-08:00","id":40011,"title":"","content":"Probably not, but aside from the implications that it's too fragile to stand up to much abuse at all, there's nothing there that nails down whether or not it's possible.<br /> <br /> Here's a question that I have: the section points out that the durations can be different for mortal and demon. Does that mean in order to get a normal cover the duration for both sides has to be permanent, or just the demon's? I can't imagine it giving out XP if the mortal's side is permanent but the demon's side is temporary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T01:37:55-08:00","id":40408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/24376-questions-about-pacts?p=37381#post37381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some sort of option should probably exist for radical physical transformation beyond the 'Striking Looks' merit... why is it that a guy can ask to be a rock star (allies, fame, resources) but not ask to be a strapping lumberjack (str, dex, sta all 4?).<br /> <br /> Seems a perfectly valid and in-theme type of wish to make, although dangerous for balance in mixed games.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I agree. That's an oversight on my part and I will bring it up with Rose. I think it could easily work like Merits, though: lesser, medial and greater Assets can increase Attributes by 1, 2 or 3 dots, respectively. Seems easy enough\u2014and has rather horrific implications if indeed the &quot;stuff&quot; granted by pacts must come from somewhere, rather than be created wholesale. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T15:56:15-08:00","id":40775,"title":"","content":"Alright, believe it or not, this never came up among my group. No one ever wanted just straight Attributes and this was an oversight on my part. For that, I apologize \u2014 more so because I can't get it into the book at this point, but I'll see if I can steal room for a very tiny sidebar in a future book. Either way, I wrote the pacts stuff. I'm a freelancer, so this isn't &quot;official&quot; as it would be if Matt or Rose or someone decreed it, but feel free to amend this as a houserule to your game.<br /> <br /> Whenever an Asset Benefit says that it increases an existing (personal) Merit by one, two or three dots, it can also increase an Attribute by that much. I'll try to help answer other questions and clear things up, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T16:23:22-08:00","id":40801,"title":"","content":"Hey, Claire, if I may ask... what's your take on Pacts removing detrimental conditions that are 'persistent'? Here are some subquestions related to that topic -<br /> <br /> Could a pact cure PTSD?<br /> <br /> Could a pact cure supernaturally inflicted conditions, like False Memories?<br /> <br /> Can a pact give 'happiness' in a surreal analogy to drug use - could I wish to be 'high' 24/7, and enjoy a new persistent condition of 'euphoric' or something for however long is agreed?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T16:42:36-08:00","id":40810,"title":"","content":"Good question. What do people pact for? Health, influence, money, things like that. Even to excise problematic parts of one's life (and then going on to learn why it's never that easy). I'd say that curing persistent Conditions could be part of that kind of thing. I'd allow it. What I'd probably do in terms of grades:<br /> <br /> Lesser: Addicted, Amnesia, Mute, Obsession<br /> Medial: Fugue<br /> Greater: Blind, Broken, Disabled, Madness<br /> <br /> I'd say that they can cure supernaturally-inflicted Conditions, yes, but the severity determines the grade. False Memories would be Medial, while Enslaved is Greater. I would say that pacts probably can't cure soul loss Conditions: Soulless, Enervated, Thrall. Though it <i>does </i>lead to some interesting implications if they can....<br /> <br /> Also, yes, I would say that a pact could <i>grant</i> a persistent Condition to the mortal, though it'd be strange. It could make a normally temporary Condition persistent, maybe: you could be Intoxicated 100% of the time. There would be no way to come down from it short of destroying the contract or maybe some other magic, however, so it'd quickly drive you nuts, I think. Something like a persistent Intoxicated Condition would probably be a Lesser aspect, because it's pretty easy to grant (and probably makes the assignee a big target for other demons wanting to forge some pacts).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":109,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","user":"Claire Redfield","date":". 01-01-2014, 07:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T01:21:35-08:00","id":40975,"title":"","content":"Thank you SO much for posting and offering your thoughts on these issues, it's very much appreciated!<br /> <br /> How about a few more oddities for you --<br /> <br /> Pregnancy, in general. Making the elderly fertile ; or, granting a person the abililty to have specifically male or female children. Then we get into the realm of swearing pacts on the behalf of the yet-unborn - essentially, Demonic genetic engineering ; I want my child to be faster, stronger, smarter. How about not only my child ; how about ALL of my descendents, to the 7th generation?<br /> <br /> Also, children in general - Can oaths be sworn by children who might otherwise be completely unable to comprehend the terms or consider the act a fun game? Could particularly unscrupulous demons clean up on souls at the playground? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T21:20:19-08:00","id":41506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/24376-questions-about-pacts?p=40810#post40810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say that pacts probably can't cure soul loss Conditions: Soulless, Enervated, Thrall. Though it <i>does </i>lead to some interesting implications if they can....</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure they can. As long as the Demon could supply the Soul.....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T23:25:09-08:00","id":41546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paddon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/24376-questions-about-pacts?p=41506#post41506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure they can. As long as the Demon could supply the Soul.....</div> </div> </div> </div>An interesting thought that. Exploits that allows a demon to steal, handle and restore souls (much like a Death mage could)<br /> Would make for a very potent negotiating tool when looking for Cover. (i.e &quot;Your daughter seems to have been broken by whatever happened to her a few weeks back, that is true, but you know, I could fix that for you...&quot;)<br /> <br /> I like that idea, I really do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T13:39:24-08:00","id":41934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MissMaddy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/24376-questions-about-pacts?p=40975#post40975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you SO much for posting and offering your thoughts on these issues, it's very much appreciated!<br /> <br /> How about a few more oddities for you --<br /> <br /> Pregnancy, in general. Making the elderly fertile ; or, granting a person the abililty to have specifically male or female children. Then we get into the realm of swearing pacts on the behalf of the yet-unborn - essentially, Demonic genetic engineering ; I want my child to be faster, stronger, smarter. How about not only my child ; how about ALL of my descendents, to the 7th generation?<br /> <br /> Also, children in general - Can oaths be sworn by children who might otherwise be completely unable to comprehend the terms or consider the act a fun game? Could particularly unscrupulous demons clean up on souls at the playground? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Good questions again! This sort of thing gets tricky. I'd say granting fertility is certainly doable. Seems like about a Greater aspect to me: it's important and dramatic, not unlike allowing the blind to see again. The ability to have specifically male or female children seems easier than that, assuming someone is able to conceive. Desperate people making pacts with demons for children definitely seems like something that could happen.<br /> <br /> The demonic genetic engineering I'm not so sure about, largely because there are limits to what demons can do. Rumors do exist of generational durations on pacts, but I didn't put in any hard rules on that because it seems like something best left to myth, rumor, and maybe a chronicle's story hook.<br /> <br /> Re: children<br /> <br /> By the rules, a mortal need not know exactly what she's signing to sign a pact. I think a case could be made for a child unable to even understand the concept being unsuitable for signing a pact. This offers some interesting implications. However, if you want to rule that children can sign pacts, go right ahead.<br /> <br /> By the way, I used to talk about one thing in particular with <b>Demon</b> being the most horrific thing in a game I've worked on. Soul pacts are that thing, because the thought of being subsumed so wholly that you are annihilated from the universe is absolutely horrific to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T16:01:36-08:00","id":42004,"title":"","content":"Yeah, we've been hitting on some really freaky stuff with this game. You've done your job. Lots of philosophy discussions around our table as a result of playing this for the last three weeks. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Thanks again for your help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T16:11:20-08:00","id":42013,"title":"","content":"Sure. And of course, though my answers are never &quot;official,&quot; even if they were, it's your game. What I want to read most is how you're getting enjoyment out of whatever decisions you make. In a Storytelling game of occult secrets and techgnostic espionage, big questions and bigger possibilities are good. Hard answers to the former tend to stifle the latter, so I find it useful to keep doors open.<br /> <br /> Sounds like your game <i>is </i>pretty freaky, yeah! Next time, I'm totally recruiting you for playtesting. You ask some good questions! I am glad to hear you've been enjoying the game. It's one I'm immensely happy to have been a part of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T02:37:03-08:00","id":53849,"title":"","content":"And the questions just keep comin'!...<br /> <br /> So what are the thoughts on a pact restoring Integrity / Humanity / Wisdom / Balance etc?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T05:44:24-08:00","id":53923,"title":"","content":"Personally, I'd rule it mechanically based on XP cost. Since a Pact can grant Merits, which have an XP cost of 1 per dot (GMC values) I'd say that restoring/granting 1 Dot of Integrity (3XP) would be equal to granting a NEW 3 dot Merit, so I'd say it would be a Medial bonus.<br /> <br /> Also note, however, having your MORAL OUTLOOK ALTERED by a Demon using a mystic pact is probably gonna worry and/or scare any even remotely sane person, so consider (and tell the player this beforehand) that this may either cause an immediate Breaking Point, or add an additional Breaking Point Trigger, &quot;Do I really feel this way, or did the Demon MAKE me feel this way?&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> However, for non-human morality traits, like Humanity, Wisdom, and especially Memory, I think the system would have to be higher, since supernatural morality traits tend to have a more extensive impact on the game.<br /> <br /> If a Morality trait (like Memory for example) Requires specialized experience (Sebayt Experience) to raise, then granting a Point is definitely a Greater (+3) benefit. Likewise, if there are system downsides that could apply, they should probably apply.<br /> Again to use Mummy as an example, since the Judges aren't too keen on the Arisen building their Memory, Doing a Pact with a Demon to gain Memory PROBABLY counts as going against your first purpose and the will of your judge, and would mandate a Descent (power stat loss) roll.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, I think the additional breaking point trigger would end up applying to most morality traits - &quot;Is this really how I feel, or is it something the Demon MADE me feel?&quot;<br /> Oh, and to be a REAL jerk, a Demon could always, say, Grant a Mage two points of Wisdom with a One Month duration. :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":509,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","user":"TiwazTyrsfist","date":".  Spacing for Readablity 01-20-2014, 08:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T17:19:01-08:00","id":54335,"title":"","content":"I have a question about transferrence of obligations from the mortal's perspective (i.e. their soul). Having just watched The Devil and Daniel Webster (an old one, but a good one), a question was triggered that didn't appear to be in the Demon ruleset.<br /> <br /> Could a demon approach a mortal whom he/she does not have a soul pact with and get this mortal to fork over a soul in place of a mortal who <i>does</i> have a soul pact?<br /> <br /> Example: Demon manages to get Daughter of attractive Cover potential to sign a soul pact. Demon now goes to attractive Cover potential and shows contract, laughs and says that if attractive Cover potential wants to change place, by all means the Demon will be happy to allow an amendment to the contract (strikeout the soul of &quot;Daughter&quot; with blood and write in new name of attractive Cover potential with siganture amendment).<br /> <br /> Why I ask is that, despite this being a bit of a trophe in fiction (The Little Mermaid pops as likely the most widely known example), the person whose soul ends up being given to the Demon gets no benefit themselves (the consideration of the contract, be it resources, other merits, etc) which seems to fly in the face of the &quot;universe editing&quot; scheme of pacts.<br /> <br /> This also begs the question as to whether the contracts themselves could be amended and whether this isn't too great a strain on what Demons should be allowed to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2059-jotun","name":"Jotun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2059_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T17:24:32-08:00","id":54339,"title":"","content":"Ooo, that's an excellent question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T17:53:42-08:00","id":54356,"title":"","content":"I think, in this particular case, I'd personally rule that you had to make a NEW contract.<br /> <br /> Contract 1: Daughter gets whatever, in exchange for her soul<br /> Contract 2: Demon agree's to void and destroy contract 1 in exchange for Dad's Soul<br /> <br /> Demon now has rights to the Dad's soul, and the first contract is destroyed (automatically as a reality edit enforced by contract 2) but Daughter also looses whatever benefit she was getting from the first contract (unless the demon and her father negotiated to include that in the second contract). <br /> <br /> Additionally, since destroying Contract 1 is the BENEFIT of Contract 2, not just an agreement but a mechanically enforced power, if Contract 2 is destroyed before the Dad's soul is claimed and he becomes a new cover, then Contract 1 in UN-voided, and the demon would have a claim on the Daughter's soul again...<br /> <br /> Also, while it's not in the Rules as Written, I'm just assuming that what amounts to A Soul for A Soul is considered an equal trade, so the contract cost ends up being the 1 willpower Dot for a Soul Pact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T18:05:33-08:00","id":54359,"title":"","content":"I can see this working through multiple contracts, and thanks for the fast replies.<br /> <br /> The only objection I have to the new contract idea is that this then means means that one Soul Pact can cancel another Soul Pact without at least one of the original signatories having control over this. That wouldn't be so bad if it didn't bring to mind the idea that one Demon could really, really mess with another Demon's contracts since the destruction of one Contract (and resulting eroding of Cover) by someone else selling their soul in a separate Contract might not need to come from the same Demon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2059-jotun","name":"Jotun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2059_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T19:31:37-08:00","id":54413,"title":"","content":"If this situation came up in my game, I think I'd rule that there would be a second contract.<br /> <br /> Amendments to the original contract would present the danger of having to physically access the contract and have it physically present for a mortal to interact with. I would think that demons would never allow this to happen given that the mortal could take action to destroy this original contract which would totally suck AND the backlash would seriously hurt you in the process.<br /> <br /> Now in regards to accepting a substitute soul via a new contract.<br /> From the demon's perspective, I would say that the demon would do their best to get out of having to void/destroy the earlier contract (the backlash sucks). <br /> <br /> I would sell it to the mortal that while this new contract is in effect I would relinquish whatever claim I had on the daughter's soul. This would give the mortal some encouragement to stay within the terms and make no attempt to wiggle out of it. If he does, somehow, find a way out of the deal it would leave contract 1 whole and claimable. As a demon it would mean that I have a loophole open that when I claim the dad and effectively discharge that contract, I'd still have the daughter's soul on the hook. BWAHAHAHA.<br /> <br /> In regards to a third party demon cancelling a soul pact between mortal and demon with their own soul pact. I believe that it would be up to your storyteller and whether they believe that mortals can sell their soul to multiple demons which would bring about it's own myriad of consequences but possibly create some seriously wicked plot hooks. Hellblazer, anyone?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1930-rixx","name":"Rixx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1930_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T19:51:08-08:00","id":54430,"title":"","content":"Another option that does come to mind from what you've said about relenquishing claim on a soul relies on whether it would be possible to &quot;sell&quot; a mortal a Soul Pact the way one Demon would sell to another.<br /> <br /> Example: Dad signs Soul Pact contract to Demon, Demon hands over old contract (with Daughter) to Dad as the new title holder. Dad rips up contract because he owns it now, Daughter loses benefit to contract but keeps soul and Dad bears a nominal consequence (lethal damage perhaps). Demon doesn't get backlash because Dad now owns the contract for a Soul Pact. Demon laughs.<br /> <br /> As for 3rd party demons and contracts cancelling contracts, the problem situation I had in mind was more of the following: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Daughter signs Soul Pact with Demon 1</li> <li>Dad goes to Demon 2, sells soul so that Demon 2 can destroy Daughter Soul Pact with Demon 1</li> <li>Demon 2 laughs, Demon 1 is mad and gets backlash.</li> </ol><br /> This way means that no one mortal has sold their soul more than once, yet Demon 1 gets royally messed in this deal while Demon 2 sits back and enjoys the spoils.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2059-jotun","name":"Jotun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2059_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-20T20:21:00-08:00","id":54443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jotun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/24376-questions-about-pacts?p=54430#post54430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another option that does come to mind from what you've said about relenquishing claim on a soul relies on whether it would be possible to &quot;sell&quot; a mortal a Soul Pact the way one Demon would sell to another.<br /> <br /> Example: Dad signs Soul Pact contract to Demon, Demon hands over old contract (with Daughter) to Dad as the new title holder. Dad rips up contract because he owns it now, Daughter loses benefit to contract but keeps soul and Dad bears a nominal consequence (lethal damage perhaps). Demon doesn't get backlash because Dad now owns the contract for a Soul Pact. Demon laughs.<br /> <br /> As for 3rd party demons and contracts cancelling contracts, the problem situation I had in mind was more of the following:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Daughter signs Soul Pact with Demon 1</li> <li>Dad goes to Demon 2, sells soul so that Demon 2 can destroy Daughter Soul Pact with Demon 1</li> <li>Demon 2 laughs, Demon 1 is mad and gets backlash.</li> </ol><br /> This way means that no one mortal has sold their soul more than once, yet Demon 1 gets royally messed in this deal while Demon 2 sits back and enjoys the spoils.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a little worried that Demon's can't &quot;sell&quot; contracts to mortals. Something like mortals not having the right metaphysical parts to handle it. So that when dad rips up the contract the demon may be on the hook. I have no sources to cite regarding that outcome, just my uneasy feeling.<br /> Though being able to &quot;sell&quot; contracts to mortals is something I haven't considered and I think it could be pretty cool with some interesting possible stories. <br /> <br /> As for your third party point, I had something like that in mind as well, and while it does really mess up demon 1 (sorry demon 1!) I don't see it as a problem. Some really good story could come out of that. The amount of work that Demon 2 would probably have to go through to (- or at least SHOULD have to go through if demon 1 takes reasonable steps to safeguard their contracts) in order to fulfil contract 2 would generally mean that, for some reason, the Dad is a really attractive Cover.<br /> <br /> I do see how it would be incredibly frustrating and a possible source of grief/abuse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1930-rixx","name":"Rixx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1930_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T13:09:19-08:00","id":55639,"title":"","content":"Since Pacts are made on something physical (stone, skin, paper), there's nothing to suggest selling them isn't possible. But Demons are careful creatures. Why would you sell away portions of your cover, that someone else could destroy at (possibly inopportune) times?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2074-64bitjedi","name":"64bitjedi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T13:15:12-08:00","id":55644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>64bitjedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/24376-questions-about-pacts?p=55639#post55639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since Pacts are made on something physical (stone, <b>skin</b>, paper)[...]</div> </div> </div> </div>And now I have the image of a pact in tattoo form in mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T13:50:15-08:00","id":55665,"title":"","content":"In that case, I'd make eight or nine &quot;dummy&quot; tattoos on the mortal. In case it ever tried to destroy the tattoo. xD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2074-64bitjedi","name":"64bitjedi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T14:43:52-08:00","id":55713,"title":"","content":"Soul Pacts (ie, whole soul pacts) aren't yet covers, nor are they part-covers, so you wouldn't be selling anything attached to you. If someone destroys a Soul Pact contract while you own it you would take the Cover repercussions as normal (which sucks), but it's not as if the soul has already been integrated anywhere. Selling a Soul Pact means you're really selling the ability to call it in and actually make it a Cover to another party (well... another Demon, but selling a mortal's soul to another mortal seems to make for good fiction possibilities).<br /> <br /> I do note that, however, there is the situation where the soul has already been called in and the cover adopted (so, mortal soul is now swallowed/annihilated) and <i>then</i> the contract is sold. This touches a bit on the question as to whether it's canon that in-use cover material can also be traded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2059-jotun","name":"Jotun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2059_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}